.TH MCPWN 1 "2026-10-20" "mcpwn 0.2.0" "mcpwn Manual"
.SH NAME
mcpwn \- intercept & tamper proxy for MCP (Model Context Protocol) traffic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcpwn
[\fIoptions\fR] \-\- \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs...\fR]
.br
.B mcpwn
\fIsubcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
mcpwn is a man-in-the-middle proxy for the JSON-RPC traffic between an AI agent
and its MCP servers \- watch every message, tamper the tool results the server
sends back, and run passive detectors over the stream. Burp Suite for AI agents.
.PP
AUTHORIZED TESTING ONLY. Use it only on agents and servers you own or are
explicitly authorized to assess.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
The available subcommands are: http, baseline, pin, replay, scan, report, advisory, payloads, templates, wrap, unwrap, init, completions, badge, man.
.TP
.B scan
Self-driving active scanner (no agent in the loop); emits JSON/Markdown/SARIF.
.TP
.B http
Reverse-proxy a remote Streamable HTTP + SSE MCP server.
.TP
.B wrap \fR/\fB unwrap
Route (or un-route) a client's configured MCP servers through mcpwn.
.TP
.B init
Detect installed MCP clients and offer to wrap one; write starter config/policy.
.TP
.B completions \fR<bash|zsh|fish>
Print a shell completion script.
.TP
.B badge
Emit a static SVG findings badge.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i 
 \-\-intercept
Interactively hold each message for review (stdio only; needs a terminal).
.TP
.BR \-r " \fIfile\fR, " \-\-rule " \fIfile\fR"
Load a JSON tamper-rule file (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-l " \fIfile\fR, " \-\-log " \fIfile\fR"
Append a JSONL session log of all traffic.
.TP
.B \-\-findings\-out " \fIdir\fR"
Write findings.json + findings.md + findings.sarif on exit.
.TP
.B \-\-guard
Run as a defensive firewall: sanitise/block malicious agent-bound content.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. A nonzero status from \fBscan\fR means a finding met \-\-fail\-on.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation at https://github.com/moizxsec/mcpwn
